  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted fusion) achieved 0.725 acc, the best result so far, a substantial jump over the best RNA-only multiprofile (0.653, config_006). However, we have only one multimodal data point, so we cannot yet tell whether the weighted fusion specifically drives this gain or whether any fusion would work. Question: config_038 is identical to config_039 except fusion changes from weighted to concat, cleanly isolating the fusion-method effect. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a minimal, single-variable comparison that directly tests whether the fusion strategy is a critical design decision or interchangeable. If concat performs similarly, the fusion choice is a low-priority axis and we can focus budget on image-encoder or aggregation effects. If concat is substantially worse, it confirms weighted fusion as a necessary component and guides all future multimodal experiments. This is more informative than testing a second image encoder or aggregation variant, because fusion is the mechanism by which the two modalities interact and we have zero prior evidence on it."
}

